		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4285&amp;p=32362#p32362"><![CDATA[
Thank you for the info! I'm sure I'm an edge case because I use the same code plug for both the GD-77 and TYT-9600, I like to edit the channels.csv to remove any frequencies that are between 199 and 300 before uploading to the 9600 (since it doesn't support 1.25m frequencies). Excel won't do that unless the fields are designated as a number, which excel won't do while the tabs are in there.<br><br>The easy work around is to use the "transform data" option and import the channels.csv into a new file and then using the save as to save the file as Channels.csv to overwrite the existing file. Import into the CPS and bam, I'm in business.<br><br>If anyone has a faster workaround, please let me know. My Excel-fu isn't bad, but I'm no Jedi Master.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=3765">KB0PCH</a> — Thu Aug 01, 2024 6:20 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
